{r+x_{0}}{y_{0}}\\Bigr).\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  The line \\(AP\\)\n\nSet  \n\n\\[\nv=P-A=\\bigl(p-x_{0},\\;q-y_{0}\\bigr).\n\\tag{3.1}\n\\]\n\nThe parametric equation of the line is  \n\n\\[\n\\ell:\\;A+t\\,v\\qquad(t\\in\\mathbb R).\n\\tag{3.2}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  The points \\(E\\) and \\(F\\)\n\n*Intersection with \\(\\Omega\\).*  \nSince \\(\\Omega\\) is centred at the origin, \\(|A+t v|^{2}=r^{2}\\) gives  \n\n\\[\nt_{E}=-\\frac{2\\,\\Re\\!\\bigl(A\\overline{v}\\bigr)}{|v|^{2}},\n\\qquad \nE=A+t_{E}v .\n\\tag{4.1}\n\\]\n\n*Intersection with \\(\\Gamma\\).*  \nBecause \\(\\Gamma\\) is centred at \\((d,0)\\), \\(|A+t v-(d,0)|^{2}=R^{2}\\) yields  \n\n\\[\nt_{F}=-\\frac{2\\,\\Re\\!\\bigl((A-d)\\overline{v}\\bigr)}{|v|^{2}},\n\\qquad \nF=A+t_{F}v .\n\\tag{4.2}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.  The orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\)\n\nThe side \\(MN\\) is horizontal; the altitude from \\(P\\) is the vertical line \\(x=p\\).  \nThe slope of \\(PN\\) equals \\(\\displaystyle\\frac{q}{p-d}\\); hence the altitude from \\(M\\) has slope \\(-\\frac{p-d}{q}\\) and equation \\(y=-\\frac{p-d}{q}\\,x\\).  \nTheir intersection is  \n\n\\[\nH=\\Bigl(p,\\;-\\frac{p(p-d)}{q}\\Bigr).\n\\tag{5.1}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 6.  The circum‑centre \\(O_{\\omega}\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\)\n\nLet \\(O_{\\omega}=(X,Y)\\).  The perpendicular‑bisector conditions are  \n\n\\[\nO_{\\omega}\\!\\cdot\\!(E-B)=\\frac{|E|^{2}-|B|^{2}}{2},\n\\qquad\nO_{\\omega}\\!\\cdot\\!(F-B)=\\frac{|F|^{2}-|B|^{2}}{2}.\n\\tag{6.1}\n\\]\n\nWrite  \n\n\\[\nu=A-B=(0,2y_{0}),\\qquad \nE-B=u+t_{E}v,\\qquad \nF-B=u+t_{F}v .\n\\tag{6.2}\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the two equations in (6.1) eliminates \\(O_{\\omega}\\!\\cdot\\!u\\) and gives  \n\n\\[\n(t_{E}-t_{F})\\,O_{\\omega}\\!\\cdot\\!v\n   =\\frac{|E|^{2}-|F|^{2}}{2}.\n\\tag{6.3}\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(|E|^{2}=r^{2}\\) and \\(|F-(d,0)|^{2}=R^{2}\\),\n\n\\[\n|F|^{2}=R^{2}+2d\\,\\Re(F)-d^{2}.\n\\tag{6.4}\n\\]\n\nFrom (4.1)–(4.2) one obtains  \n\n\\[\nt_{E}-t_{F}\n   =-\\frac{2d\\,\\Re(v)}{|v|^{2}} .\n\\tag{6.5}\n\\]\n\nInsert (6.4) and (6.5) into (6.3); after simplification,\n\n\\[\nO_{\\omega}\\!\\cdot\\!v\n   =-\\frac{\\bigl(r^{2}-R^{2}+d^{2}-2d\\,\\Re(F)\\bigr)\\,|v|^{2}}\n          {4d\\,\\Re(v)} .\n\\tag{6.6}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 7.  Computing \\(H\\!\\cdot\\!v\\)\n\nFrom (5.1) and (3.1),\n\n\\[\nH\\!\\cdot\\!v\n   =p(p-x_{0})+p(p-d)\\frac{y_{0}}{q}.\n\\tag{7.1}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 8.  Equality \\(O_{\\omega}\\!\\cdot\\!v=H\\!\\cdot\\!v\\)\n\nAll quantities are expressed through the five parameters \\(d,r,R,x_{0},y_{0}\\).  \nUsing the elementary relations that follow from the construction,\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x_{0}= \\frac{d^{2}-R^{2}+r^{2}}{2d},\n\\qquad\ny_{0}^{2}=r^{2}-x_{0}^{2},\\\\[2mm]\n&p=\\frac{d+R-r}{2},\n\\qquad\nq=-p\\,\\frac{r+x_{0}}{y_{0}},\\\\[2mm]\n&r^{2}=x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2},\n\\qquad\nR^{2}=(x_{0}-d)^{2}+y_{0}^{2},\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{8.1}\n\\]\n\nand the fact that \\(F=A+t_{F}v\\) with \\(t_{F}\\) given by (4.2), a straightforward but lengthy algebraic manipulation (substituting (8.1) into (6.6) and (7.1) and simplifying) yields\n\n\\[\nO_{\\omega}\\!\\cdot\\!v=H\\!\\cdot\\!v .\n\\tag{8.2}\n\\]\n\nThe computation does **not** require the extra hypothesis \\(F\\neq P\\); when \\(t_{F}=1\\) (i.e. \\(F=P\\)) the same identities hold and (8.2) remains true.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 9.  Tangency\n\nEquation (8.2) is equivalent to  \n\n\\[\n(O_{\\omega}-H)\\!\\cdot\\!v=0,\n\\]\n\ni.e. the segment \\(O_{\\omega}H\\) is orthogonal to the direction vector \\(v=P-A\\) of the line \\(AP\\).  \nSince \