\;-\\frac{p(p-d)}{q}\\Bigr).\n\\]  \nAll derivations are correct (the case \\(q=0\\) cannot occur because \\(q<0\\) from Step 2). → **Correct**\n\n---\n\n### Step 6 – Circum‑centre \\(O\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\)\n\n1. **Setting up the linear system**  \n   The conditions \\(|O-B|^{2}=|O-E|^{2}\\) and \\(|O-B|^{2}=|O-F|^{2}\\) indeed lead to  \n   \\[\n   O\\!\\cdot\\!u=\\alpha,\\qquad O\\!\\cdot\\!w=\\beta,\n   \\]  \n   with \\(\\alpha=0\\) (since \\(|E|=|B|=r\\)) and \\(\\beta=\\dfrac{|F|^{2}-r^{2}}{2}\\).  \n   This part is correct.\n\n2. **Solving the system**  \n   The formula  \n   \\[\n   O=\\frac{\\alpha\\,w^{\\perp}-\\beta\\,u^{\\perp}}{u\\times w}\n   \\]  \n   is a standard solution of the 2‑dimensional linear system; with \\(\\alpha=0\\) we obtain  \n   \\[\n   O=-\\frac{\\beta\\,u^{\\perp}}{u\\times w}\n     =\\frac{\\beta\\,(u_{y},-u_{x})}{u\\times w}.\n   \\]  \n   This step is valid.\n\n3. **Expressions for \\(u,w\\) and their perpendiculars**  \n   Using \\(u=E-B=(t_{E}v_{x},\\,2y_{0}+t_{E}v_{y})\\) and similarly for \\(w\\) is correct.  \n   Consequently  \n   \\[\n   u^{\\perp}=(-(2y_{0}+t_{E}v_{y}),\\,t_{E}v_{x})\n   \\]  \n   is also correct.\n\n4. **Computation of the cross product \\(u\\times w\\)** – **Critical Error**  \n   The solution writes  \n   \\[\n   u\\times w=-2y_{0}v_{x}(t_{E}-t_{F})\\tag{6.3}\n   \\]  \n   but the correct determinant is  \n   \\[\n   u\\times w=+2y_{0}v_{x}(t_{E}-t_{F}).\n   \\]  \n   The sign error arises from an incorrect subtraction when expanding the determinant.  \n   Because this sign is used in every subsequent formula for \\(O\\), the error propagates.\n\n5. **Consequences for \\(O\\!\\cdot\\!v\\) and \\(O\\!\\cdot\\!v_{\\perp}\\)** – **Critical Errors**  \n   Using the (incorrect) value of \\(u\\times w\\) the author obtains  \n   \\[\n   O\\!\\cdot\\!v   =-\\frac{\\beta}{t_{E}-t_{F}},\\qquad\n   O\\!\\cdot\\!v_{\\perp}\n        =\\frac{\\beta\\,x_{0}\\,|v|^{2}}{2d\\,y_{0}\\,v_{x}}.\n   \\]  \n   With the correct sign of the cross product the first equality should be  \n   \\[\n   O\\!\\cdot\\!v   =+\\frac{\\beta}{t_{E}-t_{F}},\n   \\]  \n   and the second equality acquires the opposite sign.  \n   Hence the expressions (6.5) are false.\n\n*Because the derivation of the coordinates of \\(O\\) is central to the remainder of the proof, this sign mistake breaks the logical chain.* → **Critical Error**\n\n---\n\n### Step 7 – Scalar product \\(H\\!\\cdot\\!v_{\\perp}\\)\n\n*The computation uses the previously obtained relation \\(q=-p(r+x_{0})/y_{0}\\) and the definition \\(v_{\\perp}=(-v_{y},v_{x})\\). The algebraic manipulation is correct **provided** the earlier quantities are correct. No independent error is detected here.* → **Correct (conditional on previous steps)**\n\n---\n\n### Step 8 – Distance from \\(O\\) to the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\)\n\n*The distance formula \\(\\dfrac{O\\!\\cdot\\!v_{\\perp}-H\\!\\cdot\\!v_{\\perp}}{|v|}\\) is standard. However, the numerator uses the erroneous values of \\(O\\!\\cdot\\!v_{\\perp}\\) from Step 6, so the resulting expression (8.3) is not justified.* → **Invalid due to prior Critical Error**\n\n---\n\n### Step 9 – Identification of the right‑hand side\n\n*The identification that the right‑hand side of (8.3) equals \\(|O-B|^{2}\\) relies on the (incorrect) equality established in Step 8. Consequently the conclusion (9.1) is unsupported.* → **Invalid**\n\n---\n\n### Step 10 – Conclusion\n\n*The final statement that the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(BEF\\) rests on the flawed calculations of Steps 6–9. Therefore the proof does not establish the required result.* → **Invalid**\n\n---\n\n### Additional Observation – Unaddressed Degenerate Case\n\n*Throughout the solution divisions by \\(v_{x}\\) and by \\(t_{E}-t_{F}\\) are performed without mentioning the possibility that these quantities could be zero (e.g., when \\(AP\\) is vertical). This omission constitutes a **Justification Gap**, although it does not affect the main conclusion because the primary logical chain is already broken by the critical sign error.* → **Justification Gap**"
