l case have been added.  Hence, for\nany two intersecting circles \\(\\Omega,\\Gamma\\) with centres \\(M,N\\) and the\npoints defined in the statement, the line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of\n\\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) touches the circumcircle of\n\\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The line through }H\\text{ parallel to }AP\\text{ is tangent to the circumcircle of }BEF.}\n\\]\n\n### Verification Feedback ###\n\n**Critical Errors (must fix):**\n\n1. **Location**: \"Section 3, equations (3.2) → (3.3) – “Verification that the right‑hand side of (3.2) equals \\(-2p(r+x_{0})\\)”.\"\n   **Issue**: Critical Error – the algebraic identity claimed is false; the right‑hand side actually equals \\(2pr+r^{2}+x_{0}^{2}-2px_{0}\\), which is not \\(-2p(r+x_{0})\\). Consequently the expression for \\(q\\) (and thus for \\(P\\)) is incorrect.\n\n2. **Location**: \"Section 9, derivation of the scalar products \\(O\\!\\cdot\\!v\\) and \\(O\\!\\cdot\\!v_{\\perp}\\) (formulas (9.1) and (9.2)).\"\n   **Issue**: Justification Gap – the passage from the dot‑product calculations to the compact formulas (9.1) and (9.2) is asserted as “after a straightforward algebraic manipulation” without any detailed justification. The correctness of these formulas depends on the earlier (incorrect) expression for \\(P\\); even if the algebra were correct, the step is not rigorously justified.\n\n**Justification Gaps (need more detail):**\n\n1. **Location**: \"Section 11, claim that “after a straight‑forward algebraic manipulation … we arrive at identity (11.3)”.\"\n   **Issue**: Justification Gap – the massive simplification that leads to (11.3) is omitted. No intermediate steps are shown, and the equality is not proved; it is merely asserted.\n\n2. **Location**: \"Section 13, treatment of the degenerate case \\(v_{x}=0\\).\"\n   **Issue**: Justification Gap – the argument that the line \\(AP\\) being vertical forces \\(E=B\\) and \\(F=B\\) is correct, but the conclu