ntly the obtained coordinates for \\(H\\) are wrong. Because the error in \\(q\\) is critical, this step inherits the same critical error.\n\n---\n\n### 7. The circum\u2011centre \\(O\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\)\n\n> Set \\(u=E-B,\\; w=F-B\\).  \n> Because \\(|E|^{2}=|B|^{2}=r^{2}\\) we have \\(\\alpha=0\\), \\(\\beta=\\frac{|F|^{2}-r^{2}}{2}\\).  \n> The centre \\(O\\) satisfies \\(O\\!\\cdot\\!u=\\alpha,\\; O\\!\\cdot\\!w=\\beta\\).  \n> Solving gives \\(O=-\\frac{\\beta\\,u^{\\perp}}{u\\times w}\\).\n\n**Justification Gap:** The passage from the geometric definition of a circum\u2011centre to the linear equations \\(O\\!\\cdot\\!u=\\alpha\\) and \\(O\\!\\cdot\\!w=\\beta\\) is not explained. One must show that for any point \\(X\\) on the perpendicular bisector of segment \\(BY\\) we have \\(X\\!\\cdot\\!(Y-B)=\\frac{|Y|^{2}-|B|^{2}}{2}\\). This standard result is used without proof, constituting a **Justification Gap**.\n\nThe algebraic solution using Cramer\u2019s rule and the introduction of the perpendicular vectors \\(u^{\\perp}, w^{\\perp}\\) is correct provided the previous equations are accepted.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Two elementary identities for the parameters  \n\n> Derivation of \\(t_{E}-t_{F}=-\\frac{2d\\,v_{x}}{|v|^{2}}\\) and \\(2y_{0}v_{y}+t_{E}|v|^{2}=-2x_{0}v_{x}\\).\n\n**Verification:** The manipulations are straightforward applications of the definitions of \\(t_{E},t_{F}\\) and the dot product. No hidden assumptions; the identities are correct.\n\n---\n\n### 9. Scalar products of \\(O\\) with \\(v\\) and \\(v_{\\perp}\\)\n\n> Using (7.2)\u2013(7.3) they obtain  \n> \\[\n> O\\!\\cdot\\!v   =\\frac{\\beta}{t_{E}-t_{F}}\n>        =-\\frac{\\beta\\,|v|^{2}}{2d\\,v_{x}},\\tag{9.1}\n> \\]  \n> \\[\n> O\\!\\cdot\\!v_{\\perp}\n>        =-\\frac{\\beta\\,x_{0}\\,|v|^{2}}{2d\\,y_{0}\\,v_{x}}.\\tag{9.2}\n> \\]\n\n**Justification Gap:** The transition from the expression \\(O=-\\frac{\\beta\\,u^{\\perp}}{u\\times w}\\) to the compact formulas (9.1) and (9.2) is